\details{
Tables are labelled as OPTN labels them. A KDPI table's reference
population is the deceased kidney donors recovered in one year, and its
label is usually that year. The exception is the table labelled \code{"2024"}:
it re-maps the 2023 donors (OPTN data as of 2024-09-06) with a different
scaling factor from the \code{"2023"} table, shortly before the refit KDRI took
effect on 2024-10-31, and is taken to be the first refit table. OPTN does
not say this on the table, so \code{formula_basis} records it as an inference.
The table built from 2024 donors (scaling factor 1.40436817065005, cited
in the OPTN KDPI guide) is not in OPTN's archive and is not stored. An
EPTS table's label is the year of its December 31 waiting-list snapshot.
The newest table of each kind is labelled \code{"current"}.
